WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:05.380
Adding ribbed bands with the machine can be a challenge.

2
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.340
If you prefer ribbed bands,

3
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.010
take it step-by-step and you'll
be happy with the results.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.940
The key to this is that knitting

5
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.900
with the ribber, we must have
even weight on the stitches.

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.860
We do this with a ribber cast on comb.

7
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.460
This is the trickiest part of this method.

8
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.540
Start by establishing how many
needles you'll need for your band.

9
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:35.260
Keep in mind that ribbing pulls in,
so plan ahead accordingly.

10
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.740
On the main bed, cast on with waste yarn,

11
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:46.080
cast on over every other needle and hang
the ribber cast on comb in the loops.

12
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.040
Knit a few rows of waste yarn

13
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.900
and then knit a row of ravel cord.
With the wrong side facing.

14
00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.400
Hang the edge of your
cardigan on the needles.

15
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.600
After hanging the stitches,
it's good practice to close the latches.

16
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.460
Using the main bed carriage, knit one row.

17
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.400
The ribber is not in work yet.

18
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:39.480
Next, raise your ribber and attach
the ribber connecting arm.

19
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.660
Transfer stitches down to the ribber
in the needle arrangement of your choice.

20
00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.080
I chose to knit 2x2 ribbing.

21
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:35.640
Thread up the ribber carriage and knit
the number of rows needed for your band.

22
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:55.540
Then transfer the ribber stitches up
to the main bed and loosely bind off.

23
00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.800
Use the bind off method of your choice.

24
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:19.160
When the band is complete,
remove the cast on comb and the waste yarn.

25
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:32.880
And you have a beautiful
ribbed band on the machine.

26
00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.120
When you're knitting on a standard gauge

27
00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.460
machine like this, you might find that
a single layer of ribbing is too thin.

28
00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.260
So knit twice the number of rows.

29
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.180
Fold the band in half for a doubled band

30
00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:52.660
and secure that bind off edge with a whip
stitch to the front edge of the sweater.

31
00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:57.700
A single band may work
for a bulk or midgauge yarn.

32
00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.920
You need to test to see
what you like best.

